{"id":"9ca2736acd4dc7e7d8c7cd923a4e15b2dfe0788a","axis":"silent","repo":"apache/camel","sha":"9ca2736acd4dc7e7d8c7cd923a4e15b2dfe0788a","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"catalog/camel-catalog/src/generated/resources/org/apache/camel/catalog/docs/doTry-eip.adoc","lines":["@@ -204,6 +204,35 @@ If there is no `doFinally`, then the `end()` should be at the end of the last `d"," "," TIP: Instead of `end()` you can use `endDoTry()` to end and _return back_ to the try ... catch scope."," ","+A `doTry` must have one or more `doCatch` or `doFinally` blocks, otherwise the route fails to start.","+","+=== How doCatch matches an exception","+","+The `doCatch` blocks are tried in the order they are defined, and the first `doCatch` that matches is used","+(the same as in Java). For each `doCatch`, the exception and its causes are matched (starting from the root cause and going upwards to","+the thrown exception), and the `onWhen` predicate (if any) must also be true.","+","+This is different from `onException` (which selects the closest matching exception type across all its clauses).","+For example, if a `doCatch(IOException.class)` is defined before a `doCatch(RuntimeCamelException.class)`, then a","+`RuntimeCamelException` caused by an `IOException` is caught by the `doCatch(IOException.class)` block.","+","+The `Exchange.EXCEPTION_CAUGHT` exchange property contains the thrown exception (and not the cause that matched).","+","+=== Exceptions that are not caught","+","+An exception that is not caught by any `doCatch` (or an exception that is thrown in a `doCatch` or `doFinally` block)","+is not handled by the route error handler: `onException`, redelivery and the dead letter channel are not in use","+for the steps of a `doTry ... doCatch ... doFinally` block. The exception is thrown from the `doTry`, and the exchange fails.","+","+If an exception is thrown in the `doFinally` block while an exception from the `doTry` (or `doCatch`) block","+is still not handled, then the original exception is kept and the exception from the `doFinally` block is added","+as a suppressed exception.","+","+=== Stopping inside doTry","+","+Using `stop()` inside the `doTry` or `doCatch` block stops routing the message, and the `doFinally` block","+is not executed.","+"," === Nested doTry ... doCatch"," "," When nesting `doTry ... doCatch` from an outer `doTry ... doCatch` EIP,","@@ -226,7 +255,8 @@ from(\"direct:test\")","     .end();"," ----"," ","-Both `docatch 1` and `docatch 2` are in the inner `doTry`, and the outer `doTry` has no catch blocks.","+Both `docatch 1` and `docatch 2` are in the inner `doTry`, and the outer `doTry` has no catch blocks","+(and the route fails to start, as a `doTry` must have one or more `doCatch` or `doFinally` blocks)."," Use `endDoTry()` to end the blocks correctly:"," "," [source,java]"],"additions":31,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"components/camel-spring-parent/camel-spring-xml/src/test/java/org/apache/camel/spring/interceptor/TransactedDoTryRecipientListTest.java","lines":["@@ -41,7 +41,11 @@ public void configure() throws Exception {","                         .transacted()","                         .doTry()","                             .recipientList(constant(\"direct:a\"))","-                        .endDoTry();","+                        .endDoTry()","+                        // a doTry must have a doCatch or doFinally","+                        .doFinally()","+                            .to(\"mock:finally\")","+                        .end();"," ","                 from(\"direct:a\")","                         .delay(1)"],"additions":5,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"components/camel-spring-parent/camel-spring-xml/src/test/java/org/apache/camel/spring/processor/SpringTryCatchMisconfiguredTest.java","lines":["@@ -22,8 +22,8 @@"," import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;"," "," import static org.apache.camel.spring.processor.SpringTestHelper.createSpringCamelContext;","-import static org.junit.jupiter.api.A